# Use Makefile for Sail commands

This project wraps Sail (and compose) through the root [Makefile](Makefile). Prefer those targets so cwd, env, and app-cmd routing stay consistent.

## Prefer

- `make artisan …` — Artisan commands
- `make test …` / `make test --filter=…` — PHPUnit
- `make pint` — code style
- `make migrate`, `make fresh`, `make refresh`, `make seed`
- `make up` / `make down` / `make restart` / `make shell` / `make tinker`
- `make composer …` / `make npm …`

## Do not default to

- `./vendor/bin/sail …` or `vendor/bin/sail …` for day-to-day Artisan, tests, Composer, or npm
- Bare `php artisan` / `phpunit` on the host when Sail is the local runtime

## Flags and passthrough

GNU Make can eat `--flags`. Prefer `./bin/make` on `PATH`, or:

```bash
make test --filter=HasAutoSlugTest
make artisan route:list --path=api
# or: make test ARGS='--filter=HasAutoSlugTest'
```

## Exceptions

Use `./vendor/bin/sail` only when no Make target covers the need (e.g. obscure Sail subcommands), or when a script/docs already document a Sail-only path (`sail-build`, `restart-db`).
